From 96133134cba7becfd21cae7a87a842dc788f264b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Robert Christie <rgcgeog@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 11:34:05 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] feat(core): Buffer.readAsync(byteOffset?, byteLength?,
 {target?})

BufferReadOptions = BufferMapReadOptions & {target?: ArrayBufferView}.
With a target the bytes are copied into it (from its byteOffset) and
readAsync resolves to a Uint8Array over exactly those bytes, instead of
allocating a new array: WebGL getBufferSubData writes straight into it,
WebGPU copies the mapped range into it, the null device likewise.
A target smaller than byteLength throws a RangeError (on WebGPU before
mapping). WebGPU readAsync also forwards waitForSubmittedWork.
DynamicBuffer.readAsync forwards the options. Exported helper
getBufferReadTarget for backend implementations.
